","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T12:21:21-07:00","id":116626,"title":"","content":"S/he would perhaps be one of the few deities to be able to have a God-born child by self-fertilisation. Don't think s/he would be able to pull off having a Scion by self-fertilisation, since there'd be no mortal parent, no mortal heritage.<br /> <br /> That the same person was both mother and father to the God-born... eh. For the Gods, it's not that odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T12:52:37-07:00","id":116646,"title":"","content":"Technically, any god with Undeniable Resemblance and Unusual Alteration can self impregnate. But most of that is not even necessary. Depending on which mythologies you draw from, there are examples of gods impregnating others by mere touch, with a gust of wind, or new divinities literally springing to life from airborne ejaculate. Whatever your story requires, essentially. Mythology is seriously non sequitur. Though it does help to stay within the general tropes of any given pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T13:26:55-07:00","id":116663,"title":"","content":"